(word "exod.20.7#10" (after "[thing]") (why "ἐπὶ ματαίῳ: substantival adjective; \"upon vain\" does not read."))
(word "exod.20.7#25" (after "[thing]") (why "As word 10."))
(word "exod.20.9#5" (sense do) (why "ποιήσεις πάντα τὰ ἔργα σου: \"do\" works."))
(word "exod.20.10#12" (sense do) (why "οὐ ποιήσεις ... πᾶν ἔργον: \"do\" work."))
(word "exod.20.12#18" (sense land) (why "ἡ γῆ ἡ ἀγαθή: the land given to Israel."))
(word "exod.20.10#15" (sense any) (why "οὐ ποιήσεις ... πᾶν ἔργον: the negative with πᾶς is \"not any\", no work at all; \"not ... every work\" would allow some."))

;; Exodus 19
(word "exod.19.4#1" (sense intensive) (english "Yourselves") (why "Αὐτοὶ ἑωράκατε: the intensive with a second person verb, \"you yourselves have seen\"; \"They\" made a third party the subject."))
(word "exod.19.4#8" (tag "V-2AAI-1S") (why "ἀνέλαβον: God speaks (from 19:3), \"I took you up\", beside πεποίηκα and προσηγαγόμην; the speech began in the verse before, so the rule could not see it."))
(word "exod.19.4#10" (sense as-it-were) (why "ὡσεὶ ἐπὶ πτερύγων ἀετῶν: a comparison, not an approximate number."))
(word "exod.19.5#22" (sense mine) (why "ἐμὴ γάρ ἐστιν πᾶσα ἡ γῆ: the possessive as predicate, \"for mine is all the earth\"; \"my is\" does not read."))
(word "exod.19.7#20" (english "him/it") (why "συνέταξεν αὐτῷ: the nearest noun λαοῦ is not the referent; the open form."))
(word "exod.19.8#14" (sense do) (why "Πάντα ὅσα εἶπεν ὁ θεὸς ποιήσομεν: \"do\" what was said, as Exodus 20:9."))
(word "exod.19.9#19" (english "me") (why "ἀκούσῃ ὁ λαὸς λαλοῦντός μου: the genitive is the object of ἀκούω, \"hear me speaking\", not a genitive absolute (\"I speaking\"); rule fault: the genitive absolute rule does not see the verb across its subject."))
(word "exod.19.9#24" (english "they may believe") (why "καὶ σοὶ πιστεύσωσιν: the subjunctive still depends on ἵνα; \"they believe\" stated it as fact. Rule fault: a subjunctive joined by καί to one after ἵνα loses the \"may\"."))
(word "exod.19.12#8" (english "to yourselves") (why "Προσέχετε ἑαυτοῖς: the reflexive of the second person."))
(word "exod.19.12#10" (english "of going up") (why "Προσέχετε ἑαυτοῖς τοῦ ἀναβῆναι: beware of going up; \"give heed to go up\" reversed the warning into a command to go up."))
(word "exod.19.12#15" (english "of handling") (why "As word 10: the second infinitive under the same τοῦ."))
(word "exod.19.12#16" (sense anything) (why "θιγεῖν τι αὐτοῦ: \"anything of it\", not \"one\"."))
(word "exod.19.16#7" (english "it having come to be") (why "γενηθέντος πρὸς ὄρθρον: a genitive absolute with no subject, \"it having come to be toward dawn\"; \"of having come to be\" does not read."))
(word "exod.19.16#8" (sense toward) (why "πρὸς ὄρθρον: of time, toward dawn."))
(word "exod.19.19#17" (english "with voice") (why "ἀπεκρίνατο αὐτῷ φωνῇ: the dative of means, \"answered him with voice\"; \"to voice\" does not read."))

